Subject: [PATCH] qmutex: unlockInternal(void*) must honour QT_LINUXBASE too

The third of these, and the same shape as 0001 and 0002: a place where
Q_OS_LINUX is used to mean "glibc on a Linux kernel" while the build is
Q_OS_LINUX with QT_LINUXBASE, which is not that.

QBasicMutex::unlockInternal(void *) opens with

      #if defined(Q_OS_FREEBSD) || defined(Q_OS_LINUX) || defined(Q_OS_WIN)
          // these platforms always have futex and have never called this function
          // from inline code
          Q_UNREACHABLE();
      #endif

so on a Q_OS_LINUX build the whole body is dead code and the compiler
removes it. The function keeps its symbol and gets a size of zero, which
means the symbol lands on whatever the linker places next — here, on
QFreeList<QMutexPrivate>::~QFreeList().

Patch 0002 made FutexAlwaysAvailable false for QT_LINUXBASE, because
qfutex_p.h excludes QT_LINUXBASE from the futex backend. That makes the
inline QMutex::unlock() take its non-futex branch, which calls exactly
this function. So the call happens, control arrives at the destructor of
an unrelated class with a QMutex* in x0, and it walks that as a free
list: `sem_destroy` on stack garbage, then `operator delete[]`, then
free() on a pointer of 0x137.

The visible failure is an EL0 data abort at 0x117 with a backtrace whose
top frame is a destructor nothing called. There is nothing in it about
mutexes, futexes or this assumption; two symbols share one address and
`nm` shows both.

The condition and the one in qfutex_p.h describe the same decision and
must be the same, which is word for word what 0002 said about
FutexAlwaysAvailable.

--- a/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.cpp
+++ b/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.cpp
@@ -843,7 +843,7 @@ void QBasicMutex::unlockInternal(void *copy) noexcept
     Q_ASSERT(copy); //we must be locked
     Q_ASSERT(copy != dummyLocked()); // testAndSetRelease(dummyLocked(), 0) failed

-#  if defined(Q_OS_FREEBSD) || defined(Q_OS_LINUX) || defined(Q_OS_WIN)
+#  if defined(Q_OS_FREEBSD) || (defined(Q_OS_LINUX) && !defined(QT_LINUXBASE)) || defined(Q_OS_WIN)
     // these platforms always have futex and have never called this function
     // from inline code
     Q_UNREACHABLE();
